spec.section:
### 3.6 Config depth — what the harness config must cover (RL-19)

The config file of §3.2 is the WHOLE hierarchy surface. Beyond the v2
fields (gateways, agent bindings, skills, responsibilities, rooms,
triggers — RL-2/RL-7/RL-8), it must cover, per agent and per gateway:

- `workdir` — where the agent's sessions run;
- `skills` — the injected skill list (RL-2), re-named here because RL-19
  requires it explicitly;
- `tools.include` / `tools.exclude` — rulesets passed into the session
  configuration (the exact per-session knob in Hermes is SPIKE UQ-5; the
  config REQUIREMENT exists regardless of how Hermes implements it);
- explicit `model` — never inherited by accident;
- `context_limit` and `max_turns` — per-session ceilings;
- `token_budget` — per-session/per-agent spend ceiling;
- `max_sessions` — the RL-14 per-agent concurrent-live-session limit;
- the RL-15 typed caps — max concurrent agents on a Hermes gateway, and
  max concurrent agents of a given TYPE in parallel.

These are the REQUIREMENTS this spec makes normative. The concrete schema
(field names, types, validation rules) is the contracts task's
deliverable and lands in `contracts/` beside this file — this spec points
at it; it does not define the schema a second time.

---
